<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  MechanoidIntrusion_AllowRivers.xml        Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-25
  ============================================================================

  The rivers of Ash'karr come from the Rust Cathedral, and the world map would
  not draw them.

  THE FAULT, MEASURED ON THE LIVE WORLD 2026-08-25
  ================================================
  Thirteen river edges cross the Rust Cathedral. None of them were ever missing:

      6486 -> 11347 -> 11342 -> 11343 -> 14568 -> 14569 -> 14564   HugeRiver
     14564 -> 2835  -> 14570 -> 14571 -> 6470  -> 11330 -> 675     LargeRiver

  The two systems meet at 14564 at 639 m, the crest of the plateau, and the
  LargeRiver falls ~300 m off the far side into the Scorch. A `Headwater`
  mutator now sits on 14564: the ancient machine vents its own coolant and
  every river on this side of the planet starts there.

  `jawa/world_links_get` on those tiles reported, after that work:

      14564  allowRivers=False  visibleRivers=0  hiddenByBiome=True
      11347  allowRivers=True   visibleRivers=2  hiddenByBiome=False   (outside)

  `SurfaceTile.Rivers` is a biome-FILTERED view. `AB_MechanoidIntrusion` sets
  `allowRivers=false`, so the links are held and simply never drawn - the river
  runs up to the purple from both sides and stops. Nothing is broken in the
  world; one boolean is hiding it.

  WHY A PATCH AND NOT A BRIDGE CALL
  =================================
  This is a BiomeDef field, not per-tile state. Nothing in the 246-tool bridge
  surface writes a def field at runtime - checked the whole list. Def data is
  built at load, so this takes effect on the next game start and not before.

  WHAT WAS VERIFIED BEFORE WRITING THIS
  =====================================
  1. The field is real and spelled this way: `BiomeDef.cs:23  public bool
     allowRivers = true;`. A patch at a field that does not exist matches
     nothing, and a PatchOperation that matches nothing logs nothing.
  2. `allowRivers` is DECLARED on this def rather than left at its default -
     it reads False in the resolved def dump, so <match> is the branch that
     fires. The <nomatch> branch is kept anyway: Alpha Biomes may reorganise
     the def, and a silent no-op is exactly the failure this file exists to fix.
  3. Eleven biomes set allowRivers=false. This touches ONE of them.

  ⛔ `allowRoads` is ALSO false on this biome and is deliberately NOT changed.
  Every Cathedral tile reported `potentialRoads: []`, so no road is being
  hidden there - flipping it would change nothing visible and would let future
  road-laying run onto the plateau, which no ruling asks for.

  ⚠️ SCOPE. This is biome-wide, not region-wide. Any other AB_MechanoidIntrusion
  tile anywhere on the planet will also start drawing rivers it already holds.
  On Ash'karr that biome exists only as the Rust Cathedral's 236 tiles, so the
  blast radius is the intended one - but that is a fact about THIS world, not a
  property of the patch.

  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MechanoidIntrusion"]/allowRivers</xpath>

      <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MechanoidIntrusion"]/allowRivers</xpath>
        <value>
          <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
        </value>
      </match>

      <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MechanoidIntrusion"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
        </value>
      </nomatch>

    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
